# SubGraph

**Color:** `#6C5CE7` | **Nodes:** 3

The SubGraph category provides nodes for creating reusable sub-graphs and interfacing between nested graph hierarchies.

## Interface

### Canvas Input

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `CanvasInput` |
| **Node Name** | Canvas Input |
| **Description** | An entry point into a sub-graph. Passes an external value into the nested graph for processing. |

**Inputs**

| Port | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `value` | Generic | — | The value to pass into the sub-graph |

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `value` | Generic | Same value, available inside the sub-graph |

### Canvas Output

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `CanvasOutput` |
| **Node Name** | Canvas Output |
| **Description** | An exit point from a sub-graph. Passes a computed value back out of the nested graph. |

**Inputs**

| Port | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `value` | Generic | — | The value to pass out of the sub-graph |

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `value` | Generic | Same value, available outside the sub-graph |

## Container

### Canvas Node

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `CanvasNode` |
| **Node Name** | Canvas Node |
| **Description** | Loads a sub-graph from a file and treats it as a single node. The sub-graph can define its own inputs and outputs. |

**Inputs**

| Port | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `filePath` | String | `""` | Path to the sub-graph JSON file |

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `result` | Generic | The output produced by the sub-graph |

**Example Usage**

```
[Canvas Node] → [process results]
   filePath: "subgraphs/calculator.json"
```
